001149r 2                       ; x = 0 repeats the last value, which is what the README documents and
001149r 2                       ; what Applesoft does.  msbasic builds a value out of a free-running
001149r 2                       ; entropy source here instead -- the Commodore behaviour -- and that
001149r 2                       ; was what this did: RND(0) returned neither the previous result nor
001149r 2                       ; anything that varied, since nothing in this machine keeps ENTROPY
001149r 2                       ; moving.  Every path below ends by storing the result at RNDSEED, so
001149r 2                       ; the last value is already there to hand back.
001149r 2  A9 5C                lda     #<RNDSEED
00114Br 2  A0 00                ldy     #>RNDSEED
00114Dr 2  4C rr rr             jmp     LoadFacFromYa
