001190r 2               ;   V A R I A B L E S ,   A R R A Y S ,   S T R I N G   H E A P
001190r 2               ;
001190r 2               ;   Inline-ported from msbasic-master/{var,array,string,memory}.s and
001190r 2               ;   misc2.s (GivAyf/SngFlt).  All MSBASIC externals are resolved here:
001190r 2               ;
001190r 2               ;     SynErr / MemErr / IqErr / SubErr / Gme        - error trampolines
001190r 2               ;     ChkCom / ChkCls / ChkNum / ChkStr             - parser predicates
001190r 2               ;     MakInt / FrmNum / FrmEvl                      - minimal stubs (only
001190r 2               ;                                                     handle literal unsigned
001190r 2               ;                                                     decimals via Fin; full
001190r 2               ;                                                     evaluator wired in a
001190r 2               ;                                                     later phase)
001190r 2               ;     IsLetC                                        - ASCII letter test
001190r 2               ;     PtrGet / Array / GetAry                       - variable lookup
001190r 2               ;     StrIni / StrSpa / GetSpa / PutNew / MovStr    - string allocation
001190r 2               ;     Garbag (and helpers)                          - string GC
001190r 2               ;     Bltu / Reason                                 - block-up-move helpers
001190r 2               ;     AyInt / GivAyf / SngFlt                       - FP <-> 16-bit int
001190r 2               ;     BasCmdClr                                     - implements CLR / NEW core
001190r 2               ; =============================================================================
001190r 2               
001190r 2               ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
001190r 2               ; SynErr / MemErr / IqErr / SubErr / Gme -- error trampolines.
001190r 2               ; The msbasic convention is "ldx #code; jmp ERROR".  Our BasError takes the
001190r 2               ; code in A, so translate; BasErrorVec (defined earlier) does that translation.
001190r 2               ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
001190r 2               SynErr:
001190r 2  A2 00                ldx     #ERR_SYNTAX
001192r 2  4C rr rr             jmp     BasErrorVec
001195r 2               
001195r 2               MemErr:
001195r 2  A2 02                ldx     #ERR_MEMFULL
001197r 2  4C rr rr             jmp     BasErrorVec
00119Ar 2               
00119Ar 2               SubErr:
00119Ar 2  A2 04                ldx     #ERR_BADSUBS
00119Cr 2  4C rr rr             jmp     BasErrorVec
00119Fr 2               
00119Fr 2               Gme:
00119Fr 2  4C rr rr             jmp     MemErr
0011A2r 2               
